# Close ports when finishing work

When you start any long-running process that binds a port (Nest, Next, Vite, Docker-mapped services, `nest start`, `npm run start:dev`, `npm run dev`, etc.):

1. Track the PIDs / ports you opened during the session.
2. Before ending your turn after the task is complete (or when the user asks to wrap up), **stop those processes and free the ports**.
3. Prefer killing only processes you started — do not kill unrelated user servers unless the user asked to close everything.
4. Verify the port is no longer listening after shutdown.
5. Do not leave background `nest start` / `next dev` / similar servers running after you finish verifying they work, unless the user explicitly wants them left up.
